# Index of H{±1} bounds the degree of F_H/F₀

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.index_le_relfinrank_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_gammaH_of_charZero`
(`d475989e-5646-55ed-a9b9-0cde5226514d`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `01eea290-07d9-510d-9b0a-1f0c9c29b20f`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and let $H$ be a
subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. For a subgroup $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ write
$F(\Gamma) =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) $\Gamma$ for the
intermediate field of $K((q))$ (Laurent series over $K$) generated over $K$ by the set
`intFormRatiosC K` $\Gamma$, that is, by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f /
\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$ where $k$ is an integer, $f,g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ for the
image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, $p_f,p_g$ are integral power series that are
$q$-expansions of $f$ resp. $g$ in the sense of `IsIntegralQExp`, and the Laurent series attached to
$p_g$ over $K$ is nonzero. Here [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) is the
subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along $\Gamma_0(M)
\hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(M)
\to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ sending $\gamma$ to the reduction modulo $M$ of its lower-right entry; so
it is $\{\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M) : d(\gamma) \bmod M \in H\}$. The assertion is the inequality of
natural numbers $$[(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times : H \cdot \{\pm 1\}] \le [\,F(\Gamma_H(M)) :
F(\Gamma_0(M))\,],$$ the left side being the index of the subgroup generated by $H$ and $-1$, and
the right side the relative finite rank of $F(\Gamma_0(M))$ inside $F(\Gamma_H(M))$, a quantity
which vanishes when the extension is infinite; since $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ is finite the
inequality in particular forces that rank to be positive.

This is the characteristic-zero lower bound for the degree of the covering $X_H(M) \to X_0(M)$ of
modular curves, realised on $q$-expansion function fields, the diamond operators indexed by
$(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times / H\{\pm1\}$ supplying the required automorphisms. It is used to obtain the
matching equality
[`ModularCurve.relfinrank_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_gammaH_eq_index_of_charZero`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.relfinrank_qExpFunctionFieldC_gamma0_gammaH_eq_index_of_charZero)
and, through it, the computation of the degree of $F(\Gamma_H(M))$ resp. $F(\Gamma_1(M))$ over the
field generated by the $j$-series after base change.

